        </ode>
      </physics>
    </joint>
    <!-- Aerodynamics. The ONLY source of aerodynamic force on the airframe:
         the LiftDrag surfaces below are disabled and the world's WindEffects
         force approximation is 0 (verified: a free body in a 25 m/s wind shows
         exactly zero horizontal displacement). WindEffects itself must stay
         loaded, since it generates the gusting wind vector this plugin reads.

         EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS MEASURED FROM THE T2's OWN MESHES, not from the
         SDF's <collision> or the old LiftDrag blocks. Both of those were
         inherited from PX4's standard_vtol (an X8 flying wing) when this model
         was built and never rescaled:

             standard_vtol   2.144 m span, 5.03 kg, LiftDrag areas 0.5/0.5/0.01
             t2_cruza_vtol   1.246 m span, 2.49 kg, SAME areas, SAME a0/cla/
                             alpha_stall, SAME collision box 0.55x2.144x0.05,
                             SAME control-surface link poses (+-0.3, -0.85)

         So the airframe carried the aerodynamics of an aircraft twice its mass
         and 1.7x its span: wing loading 2.41 kg/m^2 against standard_vtol's
         4.98. This was invisible for the whole project because LiftDrag returns
         early on `forwardI.Dot(vel) <= 0` and the apriltag world's wind is a
         tailwind, so those surfaces produced nothing at all. Removing the gate
         made them act, and a 5 m/s landing that lands at 3.3 cm with them
         disabled flew 138 m away with them enabled.

         Measured from the meshes (projected triangle areas, closed-surface
         corrected, in the model frame):
             fuselage.dae   front 0.1147  side 0.1759  PLANFORM 0.5032 m^2
                            x range [-0.690, +0.359], span +-0.622
                            planform centroid x = -0.0447
             ailerons       0.0220 m^2 planform each
             elevator.dae   0.0247 m^2 planform
             rudder.dae     0.0185 m^2 SIDE area (it is a vertical surface)
         Lifting planform = 0.5032 + 2*0.0220 = 0.547 m^2, giving a wing loading
         of 4.55 kg/m^2, in line with standard_vtol 4.98, quadtailsitter 4.05
         and advanced_plane 2.96.

         cda covers ONLY NON-LIFTING bodies now. Each <surface> carries its
         complete normal force (lift AND the flat-plate/profile drag), so a
         per-axis term over the same wing would be a second copy of it:
           x 0.045  measured frontal 0.1424 m^2 less the wing's share, which is
                    now cd0 on the surfaces. Together they come to ~0.061 m^2,
                    against the review's independent closed-form 0.0598. 
           y 0.178  measured side 0.1964 less the rudder's 0.0185, times Cd 1.0.
                    The old value (0.059) came from the X8 collision box, which
                    has no fuselage depth at all, and was 3x too small.
           z 0.100  rotors and nacelles only. The WING's broadside drag is the
                    surfaces' own sigma*(1-cos 2a) term, which reaches CD 2 at
                    90 deg exactly where the lift term is zero.

         cp values are the measured planform centroids, relative to the CENTRE
         OF MASS (-0.008481 m). The TAIL positions are the one estimate here:
         the meshes are exported about their own origins and the SDF link poses
         are X8 leftovers (-0.85 m, behind an airframe that ends at -0.690), so
         the tail surfaces are placed at the rear of the measured fuselage. -->
    <plugin filename="libBodyAero.so" name="px4_gz_plugins::BodyAero">
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <cda>0.045 0.178 0.100</cda>
      <cp_drag_x>0 0 0</cp_drag_x>
      <cp_drag_y>0 0 0</cp_drag_y>
      <cp_drag_z>0 0 0</cp_drag_z>
      <air_density>1.2041</air_density>
      <topic>/t2/body_aero</topic>

      <!-- Wing, split into halves. area = 0.264/2, AR = 5.45 (memoire 7.3.2,
           table "Parametres du modele aerodynamique": measured on the vehicle).
           WAS 0.547/2 with AR 2.84 back-computed from that wrong area.
           cd0 0.030 is the wing profile drag the old block implied
           (cda*a0 = 0.6417*0.05984 = 0.0384) rounded down, since the fuselage
           share of that is in <cda> above. -->
      <surface><name>left_wing</name>
        <area>0.132</area><a0>0.05984281113</a0><cla>4.752798721</cla>
        <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
        <cd0>0.030</cd0><ar>5.45</ar><eff>0.85</eff>
        <cp>0 0 0</cp>
        <forward>1 0 0</forward><upward>0 0 1</upward></surface>
      <surface><name>right_wing</name>
        <area>0.132</area><a0>0.05984281113</a0><cla>4.752798721</cla>
        <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
        <cd0>0.030</cd0><ar>5.45</ar><eff>0.85</eff>
        <cp>0 0 0</cp>
        <forward>1 0 0</forward><upward>0 0 1</upward></surface>
      <surface><name>elevator</name>
        <area>0.0247</area><a0>-0.2</a0><cla>4.752798721</cla>
        <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
        <cd0>0.020</cd0><ar>4.0</ar><eff>0.85</eff>
        <cp>0 0 0</cp>
        <forward>1 0 0</forward><upward>0 0 1</upward></surface>
      <surface><name>rudder</name>
        <area>0.0185</area><a0>0.0</a0><cla>4.752798721</cla>
        <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
        <cd0>0.020</cd0><ar>2.4</ar><eff>0.85</eff>
        <cp>0 0 0</cp>
        <forward>1 0 0</forward><upward>0 1 0</upward></surface>
    </plugin>

    <!-- DISABLED: superseded by px4_gz_plugins::BodyAero below.
         LiftDrag returns early on `forwardI.Dot(vel) <= 0`, so these
         surfaces produce nothing at all when the flow arrives from the
         rear hemisphere, which is most of a hover. Their parameters are
         carried over verbatim into BodyAero <surface> entries.
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-lift-drag-system" name="gz::sim::systems::LiftDrag">
      <a0>0.05984281113</a0>
      <cla>4.752798721</cla>
      <cda>0.6417112299</cda>
      <cma>0.0</cma>
      <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
      <cla_stall>-3.85</cla_stall>
      <cda_stall>-0.9233984055</cda_stall>
      <cma_stall>0</cma_stall>
      <cp>-0.05 0.3 0.05</cp>
      <area>0.5</area>
      <air_density>1.2041</air_density>
      <forward>1 0 0</forward>
      <upward>0 0 1</upward>
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <control_joint_name>
        left_elevon_joint
      </control_joint_name>
      <control_joint_rad_to_cl>-1.0</control_joint_rad_to_cl>
    </plugin>
    -->
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
      <joint_name>left_elevon_joint</joint_name>
      <sub_topic>servo_0</sub_topic>
    </plugin>
    <!-- DISABLED: superseded by px4_gz_plugins::BodyAero below.
         LiftDrag returns early on `forwardI.Dot(vel) <= 0`, so these
         surfaces produce nothing at all when the flow arrives from the
         rear hemisphere, which is most of a hover. Their parameters are
         carried over verbatim into BodyAero <surface> entries.
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-lift-drag-system" name="gz::sim::systems::LiftDrag">
      <a0>0.05984281113</a0>
      <cla>4.752798721</cla>
      <cda>0.6417112299</cda>
      <cma>0.0</cma>
      <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
      <cla_stall>-3.85</cla_stall>
      <cda_stall>-0.9233984055</cda_stall>
      <cma_stall>0</cma_stall>
      <cp>-0.05 -0.3 0.05</cp>
      <area>0.5</area>
      <air_density>1.2041</air_density>
      <forward>1 0 0</forward>
      <upward>0 0 1</upward>
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <control_joint_name>
        right_elevon_joint
      </control_joint_name>
      <control_joint_rad_to_cl>-1.0</control_joint_rad_to_cl>
    </plugin>
    -->
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
      <joint_name>right_elevon_joint</joint_name>
      <sub_topic>servo_1</sub_topic>
    </plugin>
    <!-- DISABLED: superseded by px4_gz_plugins::BodyAero below.
         LiftDrag returns early on `forwardI.Dot(vel) <= 0`, so these
         surfaces produce nothing at all when the flow arrives from the
         rear hemisphere, which is most of a hover. Their parameters are
         carried over verbatim into BodyAero <surface> entries.
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-lift-drag-system" name="gz::sim::systems::LiftDrag">
      <a0>-0.2</a0>
      <cla>4.752798721</cla>
      <cda>0.6417112299</cda>
      <cma>0.0</cma>
      <alpha_stall>0.3391428111</alpha_stall>
      <cla_stall>-3.85</cla_stall>
      <cda_stall>-0.9233984055</cda_stall>
      <cma_stall>0</cma_stall>
      <cp>-0.5 0 0</cp>
      <area>0.01</area>
      <air_density>1.2041</air_density>
      <forward>1 0 0</forward>
      <upward>0 0 1</upward>
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <control_joint_name>
        elevator_joint
      </control_joint_name>
      <control_joint_rad_to_cl>-12.0</control_joint_rad_to_cl>
    </plugin>
    -->
